# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Request a package {#request-a-package}"
msgstr "Solicitar un paquete {#request-a-package}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If other users would also need a package, [request it on GitHub](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-serverless/issues/new?template=pip_dependency_request.yaml). An accepted package is added to the environment in a later release. Until then, or for a private package, [add it as a wheel](#add-your-own-packages).\n"
msgstr "Si otros usuarios también necesitarían un paquete, [solicítalo en GitHub](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-serverless/issues/new?template=pip_dependency_request.yaml). Un paquete aceptado se añade al entorno en una versión posterior. Mientras tanto, o si se trata de un paquete privado, [añádelo como wheel](#add-your-own-packages).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: issue #2017 removes the request template, but the public PR Qiskit/qiskit-serverless#2651 keeps it. Confirm that the link remains. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Add your own packages {#add-your-own-packages}"
msgstr "Añadir tus propios paquetes {#add-your-own-packages}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To use a package that is not installed, collect its wheel files on your computer, upload them to the workflow's file storage, and install them at the start of the workflow. You upload them again only when they change.\n"
msgstr "Para usar un paquete que no está instalado, reúne sus archivos wheel en tu computadora, súbelos al almacenamiento de archivos del workflow e instálalos al inicio del workflow. Solo tienes que subirlos de nuevo cuando cambien.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build wheels {#build-wheels}"
msgstr "Crear wheels {#build-wheels}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The job installs wheels without an internet connection, so each wheel must work with Python 3.12 on Linux (x86_64). Collect the wheels in one folder:\n"
msgstr "El trabajo instala los wheels sin conexión a internet, por lo que cada wheel debe funcionar con Python 3.12 en Linux (x86_64). Reúne los wheels en una sola carpeta:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`Local terminal`**\n"
msgstr "**`Local terminal`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With `--platform` and `--python-version`, `pip download` gets wheels for the job's platform, even when you run it on macOS or Windows. It also downloads the package's dependencies, such as `python-dateutil`, `six`, and `tzdata` for `pendulum`. Because the job installs each wheel without its dependencies, upload a wheel for every dependency that the environment lacks, and delete the other wheels from the folder.\n"
msgstr "Con `--platform` y `--python-version`, `pip download` obtiene wheels para la plataforma del trabajo, incluso cuando lo ejecutas en macOS o Windows. También descarga las dependencias del paquete, como `python-dateutil`, `six` y `tzdata` para `pendulum`. Como el trabajo instala cada wheel sin sus dependencias, sube un wheel para cada dependencia que le falte al entorno y elimina de la carpeta los demás wheels.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A pure-Python wheel (`py3-none-any.whl`) works on any platform. If a package with compiled code has no Linux x86_64 wheel on PyPI, build one on Linux, for example in a `python:3.12` container. Keep the original file names, because `pip` reads the package name, version, and platform from them.\n"
msgstr "Un wheel de Python puro (`py3-none-any.whl`) funciona en cualquier plataforma. Si un paquete con código compilado no tiene un wheel para Linux x86_64 en PyPI, créalo en Linux, por ejemplo en un contenedor `python:3.12`. Conserva los nombres de archivo originales, porque `pip` lee de ellos el nombre del paquete, la versión y la plataforma.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upload wheels {#upload-wheels}"
msgstr "Subir wheels {#upload-wheels}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upload the wheels from your local notebook with `add_wheels()`:\n"
msgstr "Sube los wheels desde tu notebook local con `add_wheels()`:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr "**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each path can be a file name or a glob pattern, and `add_wheels()` returns the names of the uploaded wheels. If a pattern matches no files, or matches a file that is not a `.whl` file, `add_wheels()` raises a `QiskitServerlessException`.\n"
msgstr "Cada ruta puede ser un nombre de archivo o un patrón glob, y `add_wheels()` devuelve los nombres de los wheels subidos. Si un patrón no coincide con ningún archivo, o coincide con un archivo que no es `.whl`, `add_wheels()` lanza una `QiskitServerlessException`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upload the workflow before you add wheels, because the wheels are stored with it. They go to a `wheels` folder in the workflow's [file storage](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows), separate from your other files.\n"
msgstr "Sube el workflow antes de añadir wheels, porque los wheels se almacenan junto con él. Van a una carpeta `wheels` del [almacenamiento de archivos](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows) del workflow, separada de tus demás archivos.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Replace or remove wheels {#replace-or-remove-wheels}"
msgstr "Reemplazar o eliminar wheels {#replace-or-remove-wheels}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To see the wheels that are uploaded to a workflow, call `list_wheels()`. To remove wheels, pass their file names to `remove_wheels()`:\n"
msgstr "Para ver los wheels que se han subido a un workflow, llama a `list_wheels()`. Para eliminar wheels, pasa sus nombres de archivo a `remove_wheels()`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To upgrade a package, remove the old wheel, and then add the new one. A new version has a different file name, so if you keep the old wheel, `install_uploaded_wheels()` installs both versions.\n"
msgstr "Para actualizar un paquete, elimina el wheel antiguo y luego añade el nuevo. Una versión nueva tiene un nombre de archivo distinto, así que si conservas el wheel antiguo, `install_uploaded_wheels()` instala ambas versiones.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Install wheels in your workflow {#install-wheels-in-your-workflow}"
msgstr "Instalar wheels en tu workflow {#install-wheels-in-your-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Edit your workflow code to call `install_uploaded_wheels()` before it imports the packages:\n"
msgstr "Edita el código de tu workflow para llamar a `install_uploaded_wheels()` antes de importar los paquetes:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"
msgstr "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`install_uploaded_wheels()` installs every wheel in the `wheels` folder. If the workflow has no wheels, the call does nothing. The wheels are installed again in every run, so a large set of wheels adds to the start time of each job.\n"
msgstr "`install_uploaded_wheels()` instala todos los wheels de la carpeta `wheels`. Si el workflow no tiene wheels, la llamada no hace nada. Los wheels se instalan de nuevo en cada ejecución, por lo que un conjunto grande de wheels aumenta el tiempo de inicio de cada trabajo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Best practice: bring only missing packages {#best-practice-bring-only-missing-packages}"
msgstr "Práctica recomendada: aporta solo los paquetes que faltan {#best-practice-bring-only-missing-packages}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As a best practice, upload wheels only for the packages that the environment lacks. A wheel for an installed package, such as `numpy`, installs a second copy, and the code that imports it can get either copy. Errors from a mismatch appear only when the job runs.\n"
msgstr "Como práctica recomendada, sube wheels solo para los paquetes que le faltan al entorno. Un wheel de un paquete ya instalado, como `numpy`, instala una segunda copia, y el código que lo importa puede obtener cualquiera de las dos. Los errores por esa discrepancia solo aparecen cuando se ejecuta el trabajo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before you upload, check your requirements with `dependency_report()` from your local notebook:\n"
msgstr "Antes de subir, comprueba tus requisitos con `dependency_report()` desde tu notebook local:\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* REVIEW: dependency_report() compares with dependencies_versions() only, so it reports numpy, qiskit, qiskit-ibm-runtime, and qiskit-serverless as \"bring\", although the environment includes them (still true in qiskit-serverless 0.38.0). Fix the report, or keep the note after the list. */}\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"{/* REVIEW: dependency_report() compares with dependencies_versions() only, so it reports numpy, qiskit, qiskit-ibm-runtime, and qiskit-serverless as \"bring\", although the environment includes them (still true in qiskit-serverless 0.38.0). Fix the report, or keep the note after the list. */}\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The report gives each requirement one of the following statuses:\n"
msgstr "El informe asigna a cada requisito uno de los siguientes estados:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`baked`: The environment already provides the package. Do not upload a wheel for it.\n"
msgstr "`baked`: El entorno ya incluye el paquete. No subas un wheel para él.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`bring`: The environment lacks the package. Upload a wheel for it.\n"
msgstr "`bring`: Al entorno le falta el paquete. Sube un wheel para él.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`clash`: The environment provides a different version. Change the version that your code requires, or rebuild your package for the installed version.\n"
msgstr "`clash`: El entorno incluye una versión diferente. Cambia la versión que requiere tu código, o reconstruye tu paquete para la versión instalada.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The report checks only the supported packages, so it shows `qiskit`, `qiskit-ibm-runtime`, `qiskit-serverless`, and `numpy` as `bring`. The environment includes them, so do not upload wheels for them. The report shows `clash` only for an exact `==` version. It shows a range, such as `>=0.10`, as `baked`. The report does not upload any files.\n"
msgstr "El informe solo comprueba los paquetes admitidos, por lo que muestra `qiskit`, `qiskit-ibm-runtime`, `qiskit-serverless` y `numpy` como `bring`. El entorno los incluye, así que no subas wheels para ellos. El informe muestra `clash` solo para una versión exacta con `==`. Muestra un rango, como `>=0.10`, como `baked`. El informe no sube ningún archivo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshoot dependencies {#troubleshoot-dependencies}"
msgstr "Solucionar problemas de dependencias {#troubleshoot-dependencies}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Problem | Cause |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `pip install` fails inside the workflow. | The job cannot reach the internet. [Upload a wheel](#add-your-own-packages) instead. |\n"
"| `ModuleNotFoundError` for a package that you uploaded. | The workflow imports the package before it calls `install_uploaded_wheels()`. |\n"
"| `ModuleNotFoundError` for a dependency of a package that you uploaded. | Wheels are installed without their dependencies. Upload a wheel for the missing dependency. |\n"
"| The error says that a wheel `is not a supported wheel on this platform`. | The wheel is for another operating system or Python version. Get a wheel for Python 3.12 on Linux x86_64. |\n"
"| `install_uploaded_wheels()` fails with `ResolutionImpossible`. | The `wheels` folder has two versions of the same package. Remove the old wheel with [`remove_wheels()`](#replace-or-remove-wheels). |\n"
"| A CUDA package, such as `cupy`, fails on a GPU compute profile after you upload wheels. | A wheel replaced one of the [CUDA packages](#packages-on-gpu-compute-profiles) that the environment provides. Remove that wheel with [`remove_wheels()`](#replace-or-remove-wheels). |\n"
"| An installed package, such as `numpy`, fails after you upload wheels. | A wheel installed a second copy of a package that the environment provides. Remove that wheel with [`remove_wheels()`](#replace-or-remove-wheels). |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Problema | Causa |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `pip install` falla dentro del workflow. | El trabajo no puede acceder a internet. En su lugar, [sube un wheel](#add-your-own-packages). |\n"
"| `ModuleNotFoundError` para un paquete que subiste. | El workflow importa el paquete antes de llamar a `install_uploaded_wheels()`. |\n"
"| `ModuleNotFoundError` para una dependencia de un paquete que subiste. | Los wheels se instalan sin sus dependencias. Sube un wheel para la dependencia que falta. |\n"
"| El error dice que un wheel `is not a supported wheel on this platform`. | El wheel es para otro sistema operativo o versión de Python. Obtén un wheel para Python 3.12 en Linux x86_64. |\n"
"| `install_uploaded_wheels()` falla con `ResolutionImpossible`. | La carpeta `wheels` tiene dos versiones del mismo paquete. Elimina el wheel antiguo con [`remove_wheels()`](#replace-or-remove-wheels). |\n"
"| Un paquete de CUDA, como `cupy`, falla en un perfil de cómputo con GPU después de subir wheels. | Un wheel reemplazó uno de los [paquetes de CUDA](#packages-on-gpu-compute-profiles) que proporciona el entorno. Elimina ese wheel con [`remove_wheels()`](#replace-or-remove-wheels). |\n"
"| Un paquete instalado, como `numpy`, falla después de subir wheels. | Un wheel instaló una segunda copia de un paquete que proporciona el entorno. Elimina ese wheel con [`remove_wheels()`](#replace-or-remove-wheels). |\n"
